WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.900
Data science coding is central to many fields,

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:08.924
yet it demands fluency in specialized libraries
that create real barriers for everyday users.

00:00:09.004 --> 00:00:12.163
Code generation models could lower those barriers,

00:00:12.243 --> 00:00:16.180
but the community lacked a benchmark to measure
real progress.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:22.139
Most existing datasets focus on competitive or
interview-style problems that test algorithms

00:00:22.219 --> 00:00:24.018
rather than real-world usage,

00:00:24.098 --> 00:00:31.338
and many score answers with surface-form metrics
like BLEU that drift away from what programmers actually intend.

00:00:31.418 --> 00:00:36.844
There was no benchmark combining natural, richly
contextual problems with a reliable,

00:00:36.924 --> 00:00:39.500
execution-based way to judge correctness.
